doc:sch-1-sec-47a a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "47A Termination of employment of member of staff for serious" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "misconduct CEO may make declaration  (1) This section applies if the CEO terminates the employment of a member of the staff referred to in subsection 47(1) and the CEO believes, on reasonable grounds, that the staff member’s conduct or behaviour, or any part of it:  (a) amounts to serious misconduct by the staff member; and  (b) is having, or is likely to have, a damaging effect on:  (i) the professional self-respect or morale of some or all of the members of the staff of the ACC; or  (ii) the reputation of the ACC with the public, or any section of the public, or with an Australian or overseas government, or with a law enforcement agency or a foreign law enforcement agency. Note: See section 29 of the Public Service Act 1999 for termination of the employment of a member of the staff referred to in subsection 47(1) of this Act. ComLaw Authoritative Act C2011A00002  Schedule 1  Amendments relating to ACC dismissal powers" ;
    cof:pageNumber "7"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-act-2011-sch-1-sec-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "3 Application of item 2"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-3 ;
    values:originalText "Section 47A of the Australian Crime Commission Act 2002 (as inserted by item 2 of this Schedule) applies in relation to a decision to terminate the employment of a member of the staff referred to in subsection 47(1) of that Act, where that decision is made after the commencement of this item." ;
    skos:definition "Section 47A of the Australian Crime Commission Act 2002 (as inserted by item 2 of this Schedule) applies in relation to a decision to terminate the employment of a member of the staff referred to in subsection 47(1) of that Act, where that decision is made after the commencement of this item."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b7de86ef27794fbe5a9d25239b1917434b303d83212bf4dfed785b1b586e6213" ;
    cof:pageNumber "9"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Section applies in relation to termination of employment after commencement." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
